Subject: [PATCH 06923/11362] [outer-loop] g50t: L6 SOLVED round 9 (codex,
 phase-sync solved)

Round-9 gpt-5.6-sol session solved the phase-synchronization problem
round 8 left open. The player was arriving at each barrier exactly on
its closed tick; the fix is a genuinely legal local oscillation
(DOWN/UP or RIGHT/LEFT at the barrier position) that waits out the
runner's cycle and crosses the instant it reopens. A third toggle's
open state survives the level's third ACTION5 commit, leaving a
direct route from spawn to the target after the holders are cleared.

The source agent's own fresh-environment reproduction gate confirmed
reached_level=6 independently. The outer loop independently
re-verified regardless: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via a new
resolver priority branch, all 5 confirmed level=6,
state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED.

ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: g50t levels_reproduced 5 -> 6.
reproducible_total_levels 170 -> 171 (sum-checked;
arc_count_integrity_lint exit 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
